I've seen this house on the internet before this article, and I was much impressed by the design itself, and its discretion regarding the street scape. That said, I have a few initial criticisms: 
(1) that is a lot of stairs for anyone, especially as one ages; 
(2) the open sight lines from and through the stairs present a problem for anyone with vertigo or acrophobia (triumph of design over liveability); 
(3) as a unique feature on the street, the third floor addition works admirably, but were all the houses to add similar additions, they would eventually limit the amount of light received within the third floor structures and significantly decrease the privacy.

As to the article itself, I would have appreciated a photo or two of the basement studio and how the art is displayed in the house to get some sense of the light distribution.

